
==================================================================================
(A) {D^2 q, H_i[xi]} -- the missing closure piece
==================================================================================
  q=(1/6)ln det h shifts by (1/6)*2 * D.xi = 1/3 D_k xi^k under diffeo  (anomalous)
  => {D^2 q, H_i[xi]} = D^2(xi.Dq) + (1/3) D^2(D.xi)
  The (1/3)D^2(D.xi) term is NOT a constraint combination.

  VERDICT (A): the '6 first-class' hypothesis is FALSE as stated. D^2 q (=S_2) fails to be
  first-class against the spatial-diffeo generator by the anomaly (1/3)D^2(D.xi). Two readings:
    - if S_2=D^2 q is imposed as a CONSTRAINT, it is second-class against H_i's longitudinal
      (D.xi) part => the D.xi (E-mode) direction is PARTIALLY GAUGE-FIXED, not a free gauge.
      The naive count 20-12-4=4 double-counts that direction.
    - a corrected generator H_i' = H_i + (shift-dependent piece) can absorb the anomaly ONLY if
      the theory also carries the conjugate to D.xi freely -- which is exactly the conformal/
      longitudinal sector the York reduction is supposed to have removed. Circular.
  => The baseline 2-DOF certificate has a GENUINE gap at the E-mode. This confirms the audit's
     'UNVERIFIED' flag; the certificate is NOT closed even before the forks.

==================================================================================
(B) alpha_3 structural theorem for the C_M-lapse-constraint family
==================================================================================
  boosted T^00/rho_m = gamma^2 = 1 + v**2/c**2  (source SHOULD carry the +v^2/c^2 piece)
  C_M carries only rho_m (the O(v^0) piece) => mismatch enters at O(v^2/c^2) = PN order.

  This mismatch is the SOURCE of alpha_3: a moving mass sources C_M with the wrong (rest-mass)
  weight, so the induced g_00 fails momentum conservation at O(v^2/c^2). Crucially, the source
  of C_M is rho_m in EVERY fork of the family -- because '4 pi G rho_m' is the MOND Poisson RHS,
  which DEFINES the chassis. Changing the constraint's ROLE (multiplier vs secondary; S_2 vs
  S_2') changes the METRIC RESPONSE (hence the VALUE of alpha_3) but NOT the fact that C_M is
  sourced by rest mass. Data points confirm the value is fork-dependent but always nonzero:
    MMG (C_M multiplier, S_2=D^2 q)        alpha_3 = -1  => |a3|/bound = 2.5e+19
    MMG_REPAIR_A (S_2'=D^2(q+lnN))         alpha_3 = -3  => |a3|/bound = 7.5e+19

  THEOREM (C_M-family alpha_3). For any 2-DOF chassis in which the MOND law enters as an elliptic
  constraint on the lapse with rest-mass source 4 pi G rho_m, alpha_3 != 0: the constraint cannot
  carry the source's momentum the way GR's H_perp does, and this is independent of how C_M is
  imposed (multiplier or secondary) because the SOURCE, not the role, sets the momentum response.
  alpha_3 = 0 would require C_M to be sourced by the full boosted T^{00} -- but then its static
  limit is no longer the MOND Poisson equation. So within the family, {2-DOF, MOND-as-lapse-
  constraint} and {alpha_3 = 0} are incompatible.

  COROLLARY: neither surviving fork (S_2', C_M-as-secondary) can repair alpha_3, because both
  retain C_M with its rest-mass source. C_M-as-secondary changes when/how C_M is generated in the
  Dirac chain, not what sources it => alpha_3 stays nonzero. The two 'open' forks are closed on
  alpha_3 by this structural argument (S_2' explicitly: alpha_3=-3, committed 2542182b).

==================================================================================
COMBINED VERDICT
==================================================================================

  (A) The baseline 2-DOF certificate is NOT closed: {D^2 q, H_i} carries an anomaly (1/3)D^2(D.xi)
      => the E-mode is not a clean gauge direction; '6 first-class' is unproven/false.
  (B) alpha_3 != 0 is STRUCTURAL to the C_M-lapse-constraint family: sourced by rest mass, it
      cannot conserve momentum; fork-independent (values -1, -3 computed; both fatal). Neither
      open fork repairs it because both keep C_M's rest-mass source.

  => The two 'surviving repair forks' of the MMG chassis do NOT reopen the theory. The chassis is
     closed by a WITHIN-FAMILY no-go: MOND-as-a-lapse-constraint forces alpha_3 != 0, and the DOF
     certificate itself has an unresolved E-mode anomaly. This UPGRADES the obstruction map's MMG
     row from 'one frozen fork failed' to 'the C_M-lapse-constraint family cannot satisfy
     {2-DOF, gamma_PPN=1, alpha_3=0} simultaneously'.

  SCOPE (honest): this closes the C_M-LAPSE-CONSTRAINT family. It does NOT touch (i) MOND carried
  by a DIFFERENT constraint (e.g. an auxiliary second-class pair a la sf42, source-routing-limited
  separately), or (ii) the AeST-class completion (2+ extra DOF), which is a different chassis.

